    <TD COLSPAN=7 valign="top" rowspan="2"><!-- #BeginEditable "main" --> 
      <p><img src="images/news_subtitle.gif" width="540" height="69"></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFF99">Lands 
        of Norrath Staff Wanted!</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">I am looking for 
        people interested in any of the following jobs:</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFF99">Site 
        Co-Admin</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">I would like to find 
        somebody to help me with the main work of running, maintaining and expanding 
        the site. This will be quite a time consuming task and you will probably 
        need to spend several hours a week on the site at the very least. The 
        co-admin needs to be someone with experience of web site design, html, 
        asp and Access databases. The main tasks will be improving the functionality 
        of the site and maintaining general areas such as the News, Forums, Guides 
        and Journals sections.</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFF99">Items 
        Researcher</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">This person will 
        be responsible for the Items database. They will need to spend time researching 
        items information both in-game and on the web so that they can add to 
        and update the database regularly. This is a large task, since we want 
        the information to be as detailed, accurate and up-to-date as possible.</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFF99">Spells 
        Researcher</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">This person will 
        be responsible for the Spells database. They will need to spend time researching 
        spell information both in-game and on the web so that they can add to 
        and update the database regularly. This is a not so large a task as the 
        Items research, but the information still needs to be as detailed, accurate 
        and up-to-date as possible. It would be useful if this person had played 
        at least one caster class to a decently high level. </font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFF99">Quests 
        Researcher</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">This person will 
        be responsible for the Quests database. They will need to spend time researching 
        quest information both in-game and on the web so that they can add to 
        and update the database regularly. As with the previous two postions, 
        this is also a large task that you will need to spend a fair amount of 
        time on, especially in the beginning.</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFF99">Creatures 
        Researcher</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">This person will 
        be responsible for the NPCs database. They will need to spend time researching 
        NPC information both in-game and on the web so that they can add to and 
        update the database regularly. As with the previous three postions, this 
        is also a large task that you will need to spend a fair amount of time 
        on, especially in the beginning.</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFF00">All 
        Researchers need to have a copy of MS Access 2000 and not be afraid to 
        use it =).</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFF99">News 
        Reporters</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">I'm also looking 
        for some people who would be prepared to spend some time on other EQ sites 
        and reading through forums looking for News stories for the site.</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFF99">Writers</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">If you would like 
        to write one or more guides for the site, please contact me at the address 
        below and tell me what sort of guide you would like to write.</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">Im also looking for 
        people who might want to do some more 'creative' writing, either on-going 
        character journals that would need to be updated regularly, or one-off 
        stories or other roleplay material. Again, e-mail me telling me what you'd 
        be interested in working on.</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif" color="#FFFF99">Photographers</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">The site needs lost 
        of screenshots of items, npcs, pictures for the gallery etc. If you think 
        you can help out with this, email me.</font></p>
      <p><font face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">If you are interested 
        in any of these positions then <a href="mailto:louise.hand@virgin.net?subject=LoN%20staff">email 
        me</a> telling me which job you think you could take on and a little bit 
        about your Everquest experience etc.</font></p>
